tt-gozer (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian package. Installs the gozer command, the three Claude Code
    skills, gozer-install-skills, a man page, and the reconcile systemd user
    units (installed, never enabled).
  * The explainer site is built from real CLI output and the real history log.
  * tt-gozer Debian package and gozer-install-skills.
  * CI builds and lints the package, and a v<version> tag publishes a release.
  * gozer report writes docs/log.html by default.
  * main(argv=None) works when called with no arguments, as the installed
    /usr/bin/gozer does.
  * Suggests tt-smi instead of recommending it, so installing on a QB2 does not
    pull in an older apt tt-smi next to the one tt-installer already provides.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0700

